;; Cases of saved settings values that the two checks of the settings,
;; `BAYSOL.load_settings` (Julia) and `baysol.tui.validate` (the terminal interface), must
;; judge alike. Each case is one setting with a saved `:value`: `:valid` says whether it
;; is kept; `:expect` is the value kept (numbers compare equal whether whole or not);
;; `:mention` is a part of the reason it is refused; `:with` gives other settings a value
;; too (the rules that tie settings together need them). Both test suites read this file,
;; so a rule that one side learns and the other does not is a failing test.

